WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.380
Design rules, your brand look, and Canva on your phone.

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:09.130
This is the video for module 1 of Content Creation with Canva and Phone Tools.

3
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.920
Many people say, I am not creative. Really, nobody showed them the rules.

4
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.780
A brand look means people know your posts before reading your name.

5
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.270
Canva is a free design app, and everything here works on the free plan.

6
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.230
And master templates let you design once and reuse every week.

7
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:48.740
Rule one, hierarchy. Before you open Canva, write your message in three levels. The hook, like Fresh Zobo, 500 naira. The support, like Chilled, no preservatives. And the action, your WhatsApp number. The hook is biggest. The action is small but clear.

8
00:00:49.990 --> 00:01:02.450
Rule two, contrast. Yellow text on white disappears on a phone screen, especially in sunlight. Squint at your design. If the words blur into the background, the contrast is too low.

9
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:11.740
Rule three, alignment. Randomly placed text looks amateur. Pick one alignment, and use the guide lines Canva shows you.

10
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:25.490
For example, Bisi in Ibadan made a flyer for her women's group meeting. Seven lines of text in four fonts, a full photo background, and the date hidden at the bottom in small yellow letters.

11
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:39.310
She wrote her three levels, moved the extra lines into the WhatsApp caption, and used two fonts. A dark green rectangle at 80% transparency over the photo makes white text stand out.

12
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.670
Her sister saw it for three seconds and could repeat the name and date.

13
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:54.710
Step one. Write three words for your business personality. For example, Amaka's Pot, a catering business in Enugu, chose warm, generous, fresh.

14
00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:03.580
Step two. Choose a main colour, an accent colour for prices and highlights, a dark colour for text, and a light background.

15
00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:13.600
Step three. Write down each HEX code, a hash sign and six letters and numbers, so you get exactly the same colour every time.

16
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:26.640
Step four. Pair a strong heading font with a plain body font. Script fonts that look like handwriting are only for one or two decorative words, never for prices or phone numbers.

17
00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:39.180
Step five. Make a simple wordmark logo from your business name and a basic shape. Canva's licence does not let you trademark a logo built from its stock graphics or templates.

18
00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.780
Put it all on one page called Brand guide, and save it in your phone gallery.

19
00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:55.520
Tap the plus button and choose a type such as Instagram Post or Your Story. Starting at the right size matters, because stretching later cuts off text.

20
00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:03.000
Pick a template. A small crown icon means Canva Pro, which is paid. Everything else is free.

21
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:10.310
Double tap text to change it. Tap a photo frame and choose Replace to drop in your own photo.

22
00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.530
Tap the background, then the colour square, and type your HEX code.

23
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:25.930
Download PNG for graphics with text, JPG for photos, PDF Print for printing, and MP4 for anything that moves.

24
00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:35.690
Here is a worked example. Halima sells fabrics in Kano. She chooses Instagram Post and searches the templates for price list.

25
00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:49.620
She types her new prices: 6 yards for 9,000 naira, 12 yards for 17,500 naira, and a half piece for 4,800 naira. These prices are approximate.

26
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:57.560
She sets the background to her brand colour, makes the text white for contrast, and drops in a photo of her best selling fabric.

27
00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:07.070
In under 15 minutes it is downloaded as PNG and on her WhatsApp Status. Next month, she only changes the prices.

28
00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:17.230
To work faster, set brand colours early so they stay one tap away. Duplicate your master templates and change only the words and photo.

29
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:31.410
When you resize, say from a 1080 by 1350 post to a 1080 by 1920 story, check for text cut off at the edges. Name designs and use folders.

30
00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:44.990
To remember. One hook, one support, one action. Strong contrast. A small palette with HEX codes and two fonts. The right size from the start. And reuse your master templates.

31
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:57.310
Your turn. Sketch a better version of a busy flyer. Make your one-page brand guide. Create your first branded post. And build three master templates in a Templates folder.

32
00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.600
Continue with the lessons below.
